ust as our country was desperate for  change in 1997 we need change now  because Britain is at a Crossroads  conference  a moment of decision about what future  we all want about what we can  collectively achieve together  and about what we can be  and at this moment  what do the conservatives offer  lying in the pockets of oil and gas  Executives enriching Bankers while  families are starving attacks on our  most basic rights  be in no doubt conference they're coming  after the most basic things that we  expect decent work Fair pay the  foundations of a family life  conference so long as I have breath in  my body I will defend those rights and  including the right to strike  and when in power we will repeal the  anti-worker and anti-trade Union laws  this conservative government has enacted  all of it  Tories are not on the side of working  people in Britain today Liz truss has  already made that clearer than it's ever  been she's chosen to stun for the vested  interests for the oil companies and for  the bankers  for those profiting from this crisis and  not suffering from it  and it is working families who have been  bearing the Brunt  when I was a young mum I remember that  sick feeling in my stomach  all it takes is one break one accident  one mishap and you can't get by  and if your kids have holes in their  shoes their feet get wet on the way to  school if your fridge breaks you can't  feed your family  it's not a vision for a modern Britain  is the result of years of Tory decision  [Applause]  conference families up and down the  country this winter many for the first  time in their lives and now living on  the edge  and it's not just families that are  suffering  years of under investment have shattered  the resilience of British businesses  I think of the small business owners  like Pauline in my constituency of  Ashton who runs a local pub that doubles  as a food bank and a community center  during the pandemic Pauline had to close  her doors another small business left  out in the cold by this government  and now she's absolutely sick with worry  about her energy bills skyrocketing  feeling fear of closure yet again  local popes and businesses are the live  blood of our communities but at every  twist and turn the government poured  money into the pockets of the cronies  leaving people like Paulie in high and  dry  they need a government on their side and  instead they get Liz trust level down  Liz trickle down Liz  and so I asked Liz trust today  whose side are you on  when you boost Bankers bonuses but fast  working people to carry the can for the  energy crisis  whose side are you on  using the pandemic to power billions  into the bank accounts of cronies while  nurses while binbags whose side are you  on  when you say the working people of this  country need more graft then deprive  them of the fair pay  whose side are you on  conference I'll tell you who was on my  side when I needed it the most a labor  government was on my side when I had my  first baby and nowhere else to turn  a labor government was on my side when I  didn't have a home let alone enough  money to heat it  and a labor government was on my side  when I wanted to be a good mum to my  kids and improve their lives and I  promise you this conference that when  I'm Deputy Prime Minister a labor  government will be on your side too  I will make it my mission to spend every  penny of the public money for the good  of the nation making Britain work for  working people investing in our local  communities and talent and standing up  for this country  just as we were in 1997 we're now at a  Crossroads  the moment of choice is upon us  our movement to show our country what we  can do together  the next Labor government will pump  money back into the pockets of local  communities the people who built Britain  consider this  a third  of all government spending goes on  procurement a third  more than the NHS double the education  budget  and labor will Unleash the Power of  procurement to drive up standards and  today I'm announcing our value for money  guarantee  our pledge to ensure that every single  penny of taxpayers money provides the  best possible value to the public  we will turn the Tory procurement racket  on its head so it serves the national  interest and not the vested interests  our five-point National procurement plan  will start by rewarding businesses and  Enterprises who pay their taxes and pay  their workers properly creating  opportunities for new jobs and skills  and helping our high streets Thrive  again to unlock opportunity everywhere  and reverse the tide of young people  fast to leave their hometowns hand in  hand with Labor's green Prosperity plan  for green growth across Britain  and second we will give small Enterprise  a Level Playing Field at winning  contracts where the tour is handed  billions of pounds to their cronies with  links to tax Havens we will ensure local  businesses are no longer shunted to the  back of the queue behind Giant  corporations with more more Farm fillers  than they have workers we will cut red  tape and streamline their bidding  process giving small businesses a  genuine shot  it will no longer just be the giant  corporations with the glossiest leaflets  that wins everyone will get a fair  chance  those who put into the system  an uphold good standards will be  rewarded  and the Tories had a VIP Lane their  donors cronies you know firms with Tory  MPS on their books or anyone who could  WhatsApp Matt Hancock  we will replace that approach entirely  the only Fast Track Lane I will allow is  for local businesses and Enterprises who  create wealth in our communities and  contribute to a fairer Society the VIPs  on the labor conference will be all of  you the British public  and thirdly we will raise standards  across the economy by clawing back the  Public's money from those who fail to  deliver for taxpayers and will plow that  money back straight into a dynamic  ethical local Enterprise fund quality  and Innovation not failure will be  rewarded and by striking our failed  providers we will help local businesses  thrive  never again can we see a repeat of the  Scandal that has seen Tory ministers  write off 10 billion pounds on unused  PPE they bought with our money defective  substandard and unfit for use we'll give  the Tory sleaze Merchants their marching  orders  and instead conference we will use the  power of procurement to boost local  businesses that work for Britain  with labor they will no longer be locked  out of the system  and fourthly we will guarantee  transparency about taxpayers money and  how it's spent through a public  dashboard of government contracts it's  inspired  conference is inspired by Ukraine's  anti-corruption blueprint even under the  attack from Russia they are honest about  how they spend public money so what's  the Tories excuse they were at it again  this week refusing to come clean to the  British public and allow the spending  watchdog to assess the true damage of  the Tories discredited trickle-down  approach  there'll be no hide in places for  cronies and no corner for corruption we  will keep the receipts and we will  publish them at conference we won't stop  there  we will back the workers who are  creating Britain's wealth demanding  better for our people  which brings me on to Outsourcing  conference  the Tories have become too dependent on  handing away our Public Services on the  cheap and now we're all paying the price  we will oversee the biggest wave of  insourcing for a generation  today I can announce that before any  service is contracted out public bodies  must show that they work the work  couldn't be done better in-house and  will reinstate and strengthen the  two-tier co-creator by the last Labor  government and scrapped by the Tories to  end the scandal of outsourced workers  getting second-class pay and conditions  thank you  what conference will go further still  building on our new deal for working  people I can today unveil Labor's Fair  work standard inspired by labor and  power across the country in Wales in  London West Yorkshire the north town  greater Manchester and here in Liverpool  it will underpin a new Fair work hold  for the public sector guaranteeing Fair  conditions job security well-being  proper training rights at work and Union  access  and we will also create a fair work gold  standard to Champion the very best of  employers and the labor government will  be on the side of the self-employed too  we will give genuinely self-employed  workers the right to a written contract  and timely payment by law so they aren't  left out of pocket and chasing invoices  because our Fair work standard will  raise standards for all  and Conference  I say this to you now because labor just  doesn't have a vision for this country  we have a plan and we have a plan to  grow a fairer Greener economy we have a  plan to rebuild trust in public office  and to clean up politics  we have a plan to unleash the potential  the Tories have held back for far too  long  and the plan for Britain means we'll  rise to the occasion just like we did in  1997 because the conservatives  they've made their choice they've chosen  their side  but we are on yours and we are ready to  lead this country to better  a labor government to unite this country  through the darkest times ahead a labor  government to hand power back to the  people and the places that once powered  Britain and their labor government that  will always be on the side of working  people  the Tories have broken Britain but  together  we can rebuild it again  and make Britain work for working people  once again thank you conference  [Applause]

